duate Programs\nOffice of Graduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nThe Office of Graduate Programs (OGP) is designed to assist graduate learners in admittance\nto, retention, and graduation from the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences,\nInstitute of Public Health at Florida A&M University.\nThe OGP is committed to increasing the enrollment and completion rates of underrepresented\nminorities in the pharmaceutical sciences and health professions disciplines by:\nOffering pre-application consultations to prospective learners to answer questions\nabout the application process;\nAssisting prospective learners in identifying an appropriate graduate program area\nbased on their academic goals and research interests;\nAdvising learners about degree requirements;\nMonitoring and documenting learner\u2019s academic progress;\nProviding verification and documentation of degree completion to the FAMU School of\nGraduate Studies and Research (SGSR) and Registrar\u2019s Office;\nWorking closely with SGSR to seek their assistance in interpreting University graduate\npolicy; and\nCommunicating the College and University graduate policies and procedures to CoPPS,\nIPH faculty, staff, and learners.\nPrograms\nLearn More\nPHARMACEUTICAL SCIENCES GRADUATE DEGREE PROGRAM\nLearn More\nPUBLIC HEALTH GRADUATE DEGREE PROGRAM\nCONTACT THE OFFICE OF GRADUATE PROGRAMS\nThis office oversees the administration and compliance of rules, regulations, and\npolicy for masters and doctoral programs offered by the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical\nSciences, Institute of Public Health. Please feel free to contact us if you have any\nquestions or need additional information.\nExpand AllCollapse All\nAssociate Dean Research and Graduate Studies, Karam F.A. Soliman, Ph.D.\nEMAIL: karam.soliman@famu.edu\nPHONE: 850-599-3306\nBack to top\nDirector of Graduate Studies and Professor of Pharmaceutical Sciences John Cooperwood,\nPh.D.\nEMAIL: john.cooperwood@famu.edu\nPHONE: (850) 599-3110\nBack 